  "solution": "def longest_increasing_path(mx):\n    if not mx:\n        return 0\n    m, n = len(mx), len(mx[0])\n    memo = {}\n    def dfs(i, j):\n        if (i, j) in memo:\n            return memo[(i, j)]\n        best = 1\n        for di, dj in ((1,0),(-1,0),(0,1),(0,-1)):\n            ni, nj = i+di, j+dj\n            if 0 <= ni < m and 0 <= nj < n and mx[ni][nj] > mx[i][j]:\n                best = max(best, 1 + dfs(ni, nj))\n        memo[(i, j)] = best\n        return best\n    return max(dfs(i, j) for i in range(m) for j in range(n))",
